OL,3,GNEWSAAddiction recovery walk to bring
OL,4,Athousands to city
OL,5,
OL,6,FExactly one year ago, Steve Rowe was
OL,7,Fstuck at home with "nothing to fill my
OL,8,Fday up apart from drinking", he says.
OL,9,FFast forward 12 months, he's helping to
OL,10,Forganise a charity walk for 4,000
OL,11,Fpeople who have been impacted by drug
OL,12,Fand alcohol addiction.
OL,14,FAfter a series of seizures in 2020 led
OL,15,Fto an epilepsy diagnosis, Steve lost
OL,16,Fhis job and had nothing to do and
OL,17,Fnowhere to go.
OL,19,FHis problems came to a head during a
OL,20,Fhospital stay in August 2025 - the
OL,21,Fmoment he realised his lifestyle needed
OL,22,Fto change.
OL,23,APub: 12-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBYrk Lincs NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,382,380,200,160,0,100
